Package: selectionfragility
Title: Decision Breakdown Point and Selection-Fragility Diagnostics for Forecast Model Comparison
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Sudhanshu", "Rai", email = "me@sudhanshurai.org", role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0001-2447-0336"))
Description: Decision-oriented diagnostics for forecast model selection: the Model
    Confidence Set (Hansen, Lunde and Nason 2011) for identification of the best
    model, and the decision breakdown point (k*), the fewest evaluation periods
    whose deletion flips the pooled winner. Includes selection-as-election
    diagnostics (score vs plurality vs Condorcet winners, cycles vs ties, margin
    concentration) and a staged pipeline from a validated loss panel through
    identification, resolution, significance certification, pivot analysis, and
    run-over-run comparison.
